From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] percentage heights of an auto height as auto, images keeping their ratio

A percentage height (min-height, max-height) resolved against the
containing block's height even when that height depends on the content:
its value is then the height passed down from above, the viewport's at
the top. An <img style="width: 100%; height: 100%"> in a frame of auto
height (triliumnotes.org's screenshots) was as tall as the screen, or as
the section around it, and the sections no longer held their content:
the next ones were drawn over it. Such a percentage is auto (none for
min/max-height), CSS 2.1 10.5; an absolutely positioned box's containing
block is laid out before it, so its percentages still resolve.

An image with both a width and a height whose height so resolves to auto
was 0 high: it now keeps its ratio, as with a width alone.
